<feed xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2005/Atom"><title>News from Europe - Latest world headlines and daily news - France 24</title><subtitle type="html">FRANCE 24 explores events across Europe, including in the 27 member states of the European Union and the United Kingdom. Follow our on-the-ground reports, interviews and analyses of the events affecting social and political life on the Continent and Europe’s role in the world.</subtitle><id>https://www.france24.com/en/europe/rss</id><updated>2026-11-11T06:50:13Z</updated><author><name>rssync</name></author><link rel="self" href="rss" type="application/atom+xml" /><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.france24.com/en/europe/" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/europe/rss" type="application/rss+xml" /><entry><title>Live: Ukraine, Russia hold second day of US-mediated talks in Abu Dhabi</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:7fcb196a08ad31c11f6893e8c5e39d455beb68c8ddaa53e410fbb08421bd94f2</id><updated>2026-11-11T06:48:49Z</updated><published>2026-11-11T03:22:45Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/europe/20261111-live-ukraine-russia-hold-second-day-of-us-mediated-talks-in-abu-dhabi--18813df16781.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/europe/20261111-live-ukraine-russia-hold-second-day-of-us-mediated-talks-in-abu-dhabi" /><summary type="html">Washington called for a "new" security framework on the first day of US-led talks between Ukraine and Russia in Abu Dhabi, as Ukrainian President Volodymyr Zelensky said he was "happy" with the changes in approach by US mediators. Negotiations are set to continue Wednesday. Follow our liveblog for the latest updates.</summary><category term="Europe" /></entry><entry><title>'Europe not going anywhere': G7 summit a 'signal to Russians' that Europe is standing behind Ukraine</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:e43efc7b2980a1cc8e91b62eca34d2e8e508e911500f0892a3122833d9506716</id><updated>2026-11-11T06:49:13Z</updated><published>2026-11-10T21:57:47Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/europe-not-going-anywhere-g7-summit-a-signal-to-russians-that-europe-is-standing-behind-ukraine--7a75adc507db.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/europe-not-going-anywhere-g7-summit-a-signal-to-russians-that-europe-is-standing-behind-ukraine" /><summary type="html">As the US Midterms reshape Ukraine diplomacy, Annette Young is pleased to welcome James Townsend, Atlantic Council's Senior Advisor at the Scowcroft Center's for Transatlantic Security Initiative. "Europe is not going anywhere." With this unequivocal assessment, Townsend, taking place alongside trilateral negotiations in Abu Dhabi. While the latter may command international attention, Townsend argues that the Paris meeting carries a message of its own: European support for Ukraine is intended to remain durable, and Moscow should not mistake diplomatic negotiations for an erosion of Western resolve. The G7 meeting therefore emerges as more than a forum for diplomatic declarations. It represents a test of Western cohesion, the credibility of future military and financial assistance, and Washington's willingness to endorse a common position on Ukraine. As Townsend emphasizes, the final communiqué will also be "a test as far as what Marco Rubio is going to agree to put his name to."</summary></entry><entry><title>Asymmetric cyberwarfare: 'States increasingly use cyberattacks in support of their other objectives'</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:8df99d4cbee983353ffaca7bdd7483bb21473d1b4eda74b6ce73a0945ee5ba2e</id><updated>2026-11-11T06:49:25Z</updated><published>2026-11-10T21:25:45Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/asymmetric-cyberwarfare-states-increasingly-use-cyberattacks-in-support-of-their-other-objectives--937e2d10d52d.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/asymmetric-cyberwarfare-states-increasingly-use-cyberattacks-in-support-of-their-other-objectives" /><summary type="html">Erin Ogunkeye is pleased to welcome Rafe Pilling, Director of Threat Intelligence in the Sophos Counter Threat Unit (CTU). How can a minor cyber intrusion disrupt food supplies, expose the weaknesses of industrial infrastructure and become an instrument of geopolitical confrontation? The cyberattacks targeting supermarket refrigeration systems in France offer a revealing illustration of how digital vulnerabilities can translate into tangible economic disruption and potentially broader threats to society. As Pilling explains, “With a small amount of effort from the adversary side, they can create a large impact, in this case destroying food and producing empty shelves or empty refrigeration units in stores.” This asymmetry lies at the heart of contemporary cyber conflict, in which modest technical interventions can produce disproportionate economic and operational consequences</summary></entry><entry><title>US soldier arrested in Britain on suspicion of assisting Russian intelligence</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:c371ea5beba428f598c2c332d12d3d9e352d3c08c1d3d9779d7e054efc5f79b9</id><updated>2026-11-11T06:49:28Z</updated><published>2026-11-10T20:23:04Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/europe/20261110-us-soldier-arrested-in-britain-on-suspicion-of-assisting-russian-intelligence--9083470d25a9.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/europe/20261110-us-soldier-arrested-in-britain-on-suspicion-of-assisting-russian-intelligence" /><summary type="html">UK police arrested a senior member of the US Army on Tuesday on suspicion of assisting Russian intelligence, adding that the arrest was not related to other counter-terror investigations. The 41-year-old man was detained near the city of Gloucester, west England, and remains in custody.</summary><category term="Europe" /></entry><entry><title>What the hack? Europeans face growing psyops and cyberattacks</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:9c3e4ad0a8b936939df379b2fef2a5922a3dbb8a41e65f7baa5e3a9cd199bbe2</id><updated>2026-11-11T06:49:31Z</updated><published>2026-11-10T20:19:22Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/the-debate/20261110-what-the-hack-europeans-face-growing-psyops-and-cyberattacks--2cfcf95d4999.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/the-debate/20261110-what-the-hack-europeans-face-growing-psyops-and-cyberattacks" /><summary type="html">So this time, it's Iran, not Russia? France - reportedly acting on US intelligence - summoning Tehran’s ambassador over last month’s hacking of hundreds of supermarket refrigerators that overheated, 15 of which even caught fire. Why now at a time when Iran’s trying to break its international isolation?</summary><category term="The Debate" /></entry><entry><title>Kristallnacht' 88th anniversary: Merz says Germany faces historic test over antisemitism</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:7661c3d0da19459d2a3ade7d90f999a77c0d4a4af57754f02f08c53a8af8f3c9</id><updated>2026-11-11T06:49:43Z</updated><published>2026-11-10T16:47:50Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/video/20261110-kristallnacht-88th-anniversary-merz-says-germany-faces-historic-test-over-antisemitism--a526c9837a2b.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/video/20261110-kristallnacht-88th-anniversary-merz-says-germany-faces-historic-test-over-antisemitism" /><summary type="html">It has been 88 years since "Kristallnacht", the "Night of Broken Glass" in Europe, a violent pogrom against the Jewish population across Nazi Germany and Austria, marking a critical escalation toward the Holocaust. Friedrich Merz, Federal Chancellor of Germany, said that Germany currently faces a historic test over antisemitism.</summary></entry><entry><title>French students vow to keep up protest pressure for better learning conditions</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:6d4bcfef41a24fe01d6a867c32fb4b1fab42b7c437d753555ac8e0a2df32df89</id><updated>2026-11-11T06:49:52Z</updated><published>2026-11-10T16:40:39Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/video/20261110-french-students-vow-to-keep-up-protest-pressure-for-better-learning-conditions--a9381299c60b.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/video/20261110-french-students-vow-to-keep-up-protest-pressure-for-better-learning-conditions" /><summary type="html">France has been buffeted for months by street protests. They began in September ​with students ‌demanding the renovation of school buildings, more teachers and ⁠university reforms but then turned into broader cost-of-living protests, drawing in trade unions and political activists, and sometimes ‌turning violent.</summary></entry><entry><title>US-mediated talks on ending Russia-Ukraine war begin in Abu Dhabi</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:6a7622e481d9798c9c48ed4b83cc80738a4eac697a4abb3c02f3daebca51ae43</id><updated>2026-11-11T06:50:07Z</updated><published>2026-11-10T13:29:45Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/video/20261110-us-mediated-talks-on-ending-russia-ukraine-war-begin-in-abu-dhabi--79da08e24fd7.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/video/20261110-us-mediated-talks-on-ending-russia-ukraine-war-begin-in-abu-dhabi" /><summary type="html">Three-way talks between Russia, Ukraine and the US opened Tuesday, November 10, in the United Arab Emirates, as Washington made another push to end the war. The two-day session in Abu Dhabi is the first such meeting since February. It will focus on establishing future security guarantees for the warring countries.</summary></entry><entry><title>French students block dozens of schools, vow more protests</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:ff5cc7a4c34d893048adf6cab296d55c830998370d70ee8f301b7dce73d5fe29</id><updated>2026-11-11T06:50:10Z</updated><published>2026-11-10T13:29:04Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/video/20261110-french-students-block-dozens-of-schools-vow-more-protests--1de30cb67916.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/video/20261110-french-students-block-dozens-of-schools-vow-more-protests" /><summary type="html">French students blocked the entrances to dozens of high schools on Tuesday, November 10, as they kept up protests for better learning conditions. These protests across France have spiraled into larger cost-of-living demonstrations in recent weeks, some marked by violence and police brutality. FRANCE 24's Luke Shrago reports from the ground.</summary></entry><entry><title>France vows tough response to freezer cyberattack blamed on Iran</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:423fde15c830c10a2ade2250e17295c1f8442d4563b2f7b8934501db146292bd</id><updated>2026-11-11T06:48:03Z</updated><published>2026-11-10T10:51:57Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/video/20261110-france-vows-tough-response-to-freezer-cyberattack-blamed-on-iran--fb059c4de0f4.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/video/20261110-france-vows-tough-response-to-freezer-cyberattack-blamed-on-iran" /><summary type="html">France's Foreign Minister Jean-Noel Barrot said Tuesday, November 10, that Paris ruled out "nothing" to respond to a major cyberattack on hundreds of supermarket fridges in October that it has blamed on Iran. The goal, Jean-Noel Barrot told France Info, is "to deter anyone who might be tempted, in Iran or elsewhere, to do it again".</summary></entry><entry><title>Seniors rock the stage: Greek theater seeks to show that 'art has no age'</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:0fcd47808a781b447011006268fd2f8aa0eacf93e55c52776999865a4a5c475b</id><updated>2026-11-11T06:48:03Z</updated><published>2026-11-10T10:50:39Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/video/20261110-seniors-rock-the-stage-greek-theater-seeks-to-show-that-art-has-no-age--d63b9739c4e7.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/video/20261110-seniors-rock-the-stage-greek-theater-seeks-to-show-that-art-has-no-age" /><summary type="html">A recent Greek National Opera production afforded a group of seniors the chance to channel their young-at-heart energy into onstage performances, proving that no one's too old to learn something new. It challenged the premise that retirement means surrendering to a sedentary lifestyle and extinguishing one’s creative spirit.</summary></entry><entry><title>Russia and Ukraine hold US-backed talks after Trump says broad deal is possible</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:52da7a0f6a7dba820cee628c17a7c752aef76654e148d694d528e98a5f9d4fd7</id><updated>2026-11-11T06:48:03Z</updated><published>2026-11-10T10:40:40Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/video/20261110-russia-and-ukraine-hold-us-backed-talks-after-trump-says-broad-deal-is-possible--727bc2af7a06.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/video/20261110-russia-and-ukraine-hold-us-backed-talks-after-trump-says-broad-deal-is-possible" /><summary type="html">Russian and Ukrainian officials met on Tuesday, November 10, for their first US-brokered talks since February, after US President Donald Trump suggested last week that a broad deal was possible on ending the war in Ukraine and guaranteeing security in Europe. FRANCE 24's correspondent in Kyiv Emmanuelle Chaze and FRANCE 24's International Affairs Editor Rochelle Ferguson have more.</summary></entry><entry><title>First day of Ukraine-Russia talks 'constructive and quite substantive', Zelensky says</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:aa8e95a231ecfbaa05ea83f73304a71e556ddb7a90bc5bff894a7e56276029f6</id><updated>2026-11-11T06:48:03Z</updated><published>2026-11-10T06:09:26Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/europe/20261110-live-ukraine-russia-and-us-to-resume-peace-talks-in-abu-dhabi--54a00d669ba5.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/europe/20261110-live-ukraine-russia-and-us-to-resume-peace-talks-in-abu-dhabi" /><summary type="html">Negotiators from Ukraine, Russia and the United States met for their first trilateral talks in more than nine months in Abu Dhabi on Tuesday, as Washington seeks to broker an end to the war and Kyiv faces pressure over territorial concessions. US Secretary of State Marco Rubio hailed the talks as "very productive" and said the discussions should be expanded to include Europeans at the table. Read our blog to see how the day's events unfolded.</summary><category term="Europe" /></entry><entry><title>Zelensky calls Ukraine-Russia talks 'constructive', Rubio wants Europe 'at the table'</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:8f93c0f774b532e741c6141e6b5e9cfe1e2a130175ed92ab53eb771d5648669d</id><updated>2026-11-11T06:50:13Z</updated><published>2026-11-10T03:01:55Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/europe/20261110-zelensky-calls-ukraine-russia-talks-constructive-rubio-wants-europe-at-the-table--4f2497198512.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/europe/20261110-zelensky-calls-ukraine-russia-talks-constructive-rubio-wants-europe-at-the-table" /><summary type="html">US Secretary of State Marco Rubio on Tuesday hailed US-mediated talks between Russia and Ukraine in Abu Dhabi as "very productive" and said the discussions should be expanded to include Europeans at the table. Ukraine's Volodymyr Zelensky described the talks as "constructive and quite substantive", adding that negotiators were working on a possible major exchange of prisoners.</summary><category term="Europe" /></entry><entry><title>UK writer M. John Harrison wins Booker Prize for AI-tinged apocalyptic novel</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:2670fcd7f9c109c38f3da30b339882f4579da5ed812792881447a15830e4b984</id><updated>2026-11-11T06:48:03Z</updated><published>2026-11-09T22:09:55Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/europe/20261109-uk-writer-m-john-harrison-wins-booker-prize-for-ai-tinged-apocalyptic-novel--baced25ef4ad.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/europe/20261109-uk-writer-m-john-harrison-wins-booker-prize-for-ai-tinged-apocalyptic-novel" /><summary type="html">UK author M. John Harrison won the Booker Prize on Monday for his enigmatic novel "The End of Everything", which echoes concerns about artificial intelligence in a darkly satirical depiction of post-apocalyptic Britain.</summary><category term="Europe" /></entry><entry><title>What to expect as Russia, Ukraine and the US hold trilateral talks in Abu Dhabi</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:882f0d33a601e69bb1511342fdf25493f985cc8785e4bd8c8c31cc86ac8b1601</id><updated>2026-11-11T06:48:03Z</updated><published>2026-11-09T21:46:23Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/europe/20261109-what-to-expect-as-russia-ukraine-and-us-hold-trilateral-talks-in-abu-dhabi--07b759c50f93.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/europe/20261109-what-to-expect-as-russia-ukraine-and-us-hold-trilateral-talks-in-abu-dhabi" /><summary type="html">Negotiators from Ukraine, Russia and the United States are set to meet in the capital of the United Arab Emirates (UAE) on Tuesday for a new round of talks aimed at ending nearly five years of full-scale war triggered by Moscow's invasion of its neighbour. Security guarantees for the warring sides are set to top the agenda, with US officials insisting that a broader security architecture for Europe must be part of any peace deal.</summary><category term="Europe" /></entry><entry><title>Paris prosecutor opens probe into IRGC cyber unit Shahid Kaveh over fridge cyberattacks</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:e5e1da75d7440c67a2070df111f9b863eea27c6ac39e66824fc43c3dd186bf8b</id><updated>2026-11-11T06:48:03Z</updated><published>2026-11-09T20:06:09Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/paris-prosecutor-opens-probe-into-irgc-cyber-unit-shahid-kaveh-over-fridge-cyberattacks--f78cb38b635a.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/paris-prosecutor-opens-probe-into-irgc-cyber-unit-shahid-kaveh-over-fridge-cyberattacks" /><summary type="html">The Paris prosecutor said she had opened an investigation into Shahid Kaveh, a shadowy cyber unit of the IRGC, the Islamic republic's ideological army, over the 'unprecedented' cyberattacks targeting French supermarkets' fridges in October. Little is known about the Shahid Kaveh unit, although analysts have long observed that the IRGC, which has a vast network of operations, had actively branched out into cyber warfare in recent years. FRANCE 24's Reza Sayah reports from Tehran.</summary></entry><entry><title>'Sexual predator' Russell Brand jailed for 10 years for rape, assault</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:3d6ebbc8049af01236b565b2734ea98fbf644b0c1a465c83960477e59e42462c</id><updated>2026-11-11T06:48:03Z</updated><published>2026-11-09T20:03:55Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/sexual-predator-russell-brand-jailed-for-10-years-for-rape-assault--03265434b707.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/sexual-predator-russell-brand-jailed-for-10-years-for-rape-assault" /><summary type="html">British comedian and TV star Russell Brand was Monday jailed for more than 10 years for a string of sex offences including rape, as the judge told him he had been a "sexual predator" whose fame had protected him. Brand, 51, showed no emotion as judge Joel Bennathan said he had acted with "staggering arrogance" and shown "contempt" for his victims, who had suffered significant and lasting harm. FRANCE 24's Carys Garland reports.</summary></entry><entry><title>French PM brings forward hike in minimum wage to calm protesters</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:ccb1b41196c20c63946795e88c200f426e811b7480dbe7e1c23f831eba6253ab</id><updated>2026-11-11T06:48:03Z</updated><published>2026-11-09T16:47:54Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/video/20261109-french-pm-brings-forward-hike-in-minimum-wage-to-calm-protesters--1f3e775b1585.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/video/20261109-french-pm-brings-forward-hike-in-minimum-wage-to-calm-protesters" /><summary type="html">French Prime Minister Sebastien Lecornu said ​on Monday, November 9, he was bringing forward a planned hike in the minimum wage to December from January, as he sought to defuse a cost-of-living crisis that has sparked some of France's worst civil unrest in years. Unions swiftly dismissed the offer as "crumbs".</summary></entry><entry><title>France accuses Iran of hacking supermarket fridges</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:66a3793ef886f77bf6289598a35cdd5b0e865336c25fe07a2ee0ffd086815a41</id><updated>2026-11-11T06:48:03Z</updated><published>2026-11-09T16:42:07Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/europe/20261109-iran-revolutionary-guards-behind-cyberattacks-on-supermarket-fridges-says-french-fm-barrot--977c1baab94e.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/europe/20261109-iran-revolutionary-guards-behind-cyberattacks-on-supermarket-fridges-says-french-fm-barrot" /><summary type="html">French Foreign Minister Jean-Noël Barrot on Monday accused Iran's Revolutionary Guards of being behind a recent cyberattack on French supermarket fridges, saying there would be consequences for the country. The Paris prosecutor's office said it had opened an investigation into an Iranian cyber unit affiliated with the Guards over the cyberattacks.</summary><category term="Europe" /></entry><entry><title>'Sexual predator' Russell Brand jailed for 10 years for rape, assault</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:c95e72b4062693fce9597b6a687e82fdf5420c16ee341d2b576046d449f02204</id><updated>2026-11-11T06:48:03Z</updated><published>2026-11-09T16:16:54Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/video/20261109-sexual-predator-russell-brand-jailed-for-10-years-for-rape-assault--8261ff0a2a6f.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/video/20261109-sexual-predator-russell-brand-jailed-for-10-years-for-rape-assault" /><summary type="html">British comedian and TV star Russell Brand was Monday jailed for more than 10 years for a string of sex offences including rape as the judge told him he had been a "sexual predator" whose fame had protected him.</summary></entry><entry><title>Spain's right holds poll lead over Sanchez's Socialists ahead of November 29 snap election</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:3d78dcf6307305474910668be5989b7b21cf40e2179d3f8220cb24d8a4fd770c</id><updated>2026-11-11T06:48:03Z</updated><published>2026-11-09T15:46:54Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/europe/20261109-spain-right-leads-sanchez-socialists-in-polls-for-november-29-snap-election--1d062be0599a.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/europe/20261109-spain-right-leads-sanchez-socialists-in-polls-for-november-29-snap-election" /><summary type="html">Spain's ruling Socialists have narrowed the gap but continue to trail the conservative People's Party, who would need to team up with the far-right Vox party to secure a majority of seats in parliament, pollsters say with three weeks to go before the country's general election.</summary><category term="Europe" /></entry><entry><title>Shock and grief in Poland after weekend mass shooting</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:f37badd7e7358bb0002f2d2ae33ac4fc277f3f8d1d2b15f0523e2a9ebecaa067</id><updated>2026-11-11T06:48:03Z</updated><published>2026-11-09T15:31:45Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/video/20261109-shock-and-grief-in-poland-after-weekend-mass-shooting--e6f1c827a5aa.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/video/20261109-shock-and-grief-in-poland-after-weekend-mass-shooting" /><summary type="html">Poland was in shock after a weekend mass shooting in which a gunman opened fire, killing six people and wounding 15 in the city of Krakow before police shot and wounded him. The shooter died in the hospital on Monday morning, police said.</summary></entry><entry><title>Russell Brand sentenced to 10 years, 6 months for rape and sexual assault</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:657a1c8220910dca846bcba44a91f29b5ce7b719940e54cfd436cb6814db276a</id><updated>2026-11-11T06:48:03Z</updated><published>2026-11-09T14:45:15Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/europe/20261109-russell-brand-sentenced-to-10-years-6-months-for-rape-and-sexual-assault--3be1a4c1e376.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/europe/20261109-russell-brand-sentenced-to-10-years-6-months-for-rape-and-sexual-assault" /><summary type="html">Comedian Russell ​Brand, once one ‌of Britain's most high-profile broadcasters, ⁠was sentenced to 10-and-a-half years in prison on Monday after he was convicted of raping one woman and ‌sexually assaulting three more around two decades ago.</summary><category term="Europe" /></entry><entry><title>Saving the Venetian lagoon: A natural buffer against climate change</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:434fe329b208f1cee2e12bb2be9483307c1a98c16899c92cbeeeca55bf0573d5</id><updated>2026-11-11T06:48:03Z</updated><published>2026-11-09T14:18:52Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/focus/20261109-saving-the-venetian-lagoon-a-natural-buffer-against-climate-change--0c07a9ddcfbf.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/focus/20261109-saving-the-venetian-lagoon-a-natural-buffer-against-climate-change" /><summary type="html">The Venetian lagoon is home to "barene" – salt marshes made of vegetation and mud, which play an important role against the effects of climate breakdown. They absorb CO2 and can store it long term in the soil, even more efficiently than land forests. But erosion and rising sea levels are threatening these natural ramparts. Today, scientists and environmental associations are trying to save these unique ecosystems. Our Italy correspondent Natalia Mendoza reports.</summary><category term="Focus" /></entry><entry><title>COP31: A focus on electrification as extreme weather events shake the world</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:3a851538f9a0bad5ec92b7ba976886fa7ae7760194ba9e14da2e341ce72d312c</id><updated>2026-11-11T06:48:03Z</updated><published>2026-11-09T13:35:25Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/video/20261109-cop31-a-focus-on-electrification-as-extreme-weather-events-shake-the-world--66e99fbb063b.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/video/20261109-cop31-a-focus-on-electrification-as-extreme-weather-events-shake-the-world" /><summary type="html">Most of the world’s countries are gathering this week for COP31 in Antalya, Turkey. This United Nations Climate Change Conference opens amid deep concern following extreme weather events such as the deadly floods in Nepal and a supersized El Niño. Experts say that in uncertain times, it is even more important to accelerate global efforts.</summary></entry><entry><title>French policemen go on trial over 2020 beating of Black music producer</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:fdf70b2bf1b86f959416ff2ebf99d22738593c787f933ce5b8b21fe2343d48d6</id><updated>2026-11-11T06:48:03Z</updated><published>2026-11-09T11:38:20Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/video/20261109-french-policemen-go-on-trial-over-2020-beating-of-black-music-producer--eb4ea46f0e38.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/video/20261109-french-policemen-go-on-trial-over-2020-beating-of-black-music-producer" /><summary type="html">Three French policemen went on trial on Monday, November 9, over the beating of a Black music producer they say was not wearing a face mask during the Covid pandemic, in a rare police brutality case to go to court. The assault on Michel Zecler, now 47, triggered renewed outrage in France over police violence, which victims and researchers say is systemic.</summary></entry><entry><title>French PM Lecornu holds talks over protesters' cost-of-living concerns</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:35b6c2b5e71f42441902405df885cd8c813e50c6fa26f331751fb48863c09b3c</id><updated>2026-11-11T06:48:03Z</updated><published>2026-11-09T10:40:01Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/video/20261109-french-pm-lecornu-holds-talks-over-protesters-cost-of-living-concerns--4e605f80054d.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/video/20261109-french-pm-lecornu-holds-talks-over-protesters-cost-of-living-concerns" /><summary type="html">French Prime ⁠Minister Sebastien Lecornu is set to meet ​representatives of employers' organisations and private-sector unions on Monday, November 9, to try ​to address cost-of-living concerns that have sparked some of France's worst civil unrest in years.</summary></entry><entry><title>Poland begins 2 days of national mourning after gunman kills 6</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:31dc563fc01000934b81e74f0fd8781924caf4f934d1f388db4601eb604edc60</id><updated>2026-11-11T06:48:03Z</updated><published>2026-11-09T10:37:02Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/video/20261109-poland-begins-2-days-of-national-mourning-after-gunman-kills-6--0409be610d4c.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/video/20261109-poland-begins-2-days-of-national-mourning-after-gunman-kills-6" /><summary type="html">Poland has begun two days of national mourning after a gunman opened fire in Krakow's main square Saturday afternoon, November 7. Six people were killed and at least 15 were injured. The gunman was shot and detained by police. He then died later in hospital.</summary></entry><entry><title>European troops in Poland: 'Coalition of the Willing' holds military exercises</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:840fc74b6205508f4d0bf237b04245d986f181ea7f6ba98c303f0295edfb6db5</id><updated>2026-11-11T06:48:03Z</updated><published>2026-11-09T09:53:53Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/video/20261109-european-troops-in-poland-coalition-of-the-willing-holds-military-exercises--962b498289fb.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/video/20261109-european-troops-in-poland-coalition-of-the-willing-holds-military-exercises" /><summary type="html">Some 2,800 troops from 10 different European countries are taking part in a multinational military exercise in Poland.  The aim is to prepare European forces for a possible deployment to Ukraine after hostilities end.</summary></entry></feed>
